    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Adélie penguins are the most "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " penguins in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Antarctica",
            "zh": "南极洲"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". But why are they able to live there so well? Read on to learn some of the secrets of their bodies!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Adélie penguins have "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "webbed",
            "zh": "有蹼的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " feet. They use their feet and small wings to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " in the water. They also have nails on their feet. The penguins usually nest on "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "rocky cliffs",
            "zh": "嶙峋的悬崖"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Their nails help them "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the cliffs."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The penguins’ feathers keep them "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and dry. The bottoms of their feathers are fluffy. This helps them to hold in their body "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". The tops of their feathers are "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "stiff",
            "ref": "v-stiff"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " and have tiny pieces on them. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " these pieces, the feathers are able to join together and form a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "barrier",
            "zh": "屏障"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This way, water can’t "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the penguins’ skin."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The penguins drink salty seawater and eat food full of salt. Most other animals would become "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " after eating so much salt. These penguins, "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", have special "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "glands",
            "zh": "腺体"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " above their eyes. These glands help the penguins’ bodies "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the salt. When the birds "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "sneeze",
            "ref": "v-sneeze"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " or shake their heads, drops of salty water come out of their noses. This can sometimes make them look like they have "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "runny noses",
            "ref": "v-runny-nose"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
